//
// PROBE: the last words no corpus program spells.
//
// Nothing here shares a subject — this is the tail of the vocabulary, gathered
// so that every word Bund2 implements is run against the oracle at least once.
// Several are aliases whose only interesting property is that they resolve to
// the right target, which a probe is the only way to state.
//
// Two words are **deliberately absent** and carried as Q22 instead:
//
//   - `drop_stack` removes the current stack, and the reference then names the
//     next one with a **fresh nanoid** — a different string every run, so no
//     golden can hold it.
//   - `endcontext` errors in Bund2 where the reference succeeds, and the cause
//     is context bookkeeping rather than the word.
//
// `?move`'s operand order is the deep one: `<name> <value> <lambda> ?move`.
// The lambda runs *first*, its result is the condition, and the value moves
// only if that was true — so the value is pulled from under an answer the
// lambda may have pushed from anywhere
// (reference/rust_multistackvm/src/stdlib/stackop/conditional_move.rs:16-45).
//
// `stacks_left` and its aliases `<-` and `←` are absent for F71: the reference
// registers only the function form, so the bare word is unreachable there.
//
"probe: rotate_current aliases move values within one stack" println
1 2 3 --> debug.display_stack
clear
1 2 3 <-- debug.display_stack
clear

"probe: the right-arrow alias walks the stack ring" println
:t ensure_stack
@main
→ current println
@main

"probe: set spelled as an element-of sign" println
dict "k" 9 ∈ println

"probe: ?error builds a CONDITIONAL" println
?error type println drop

"probe: space prints one, between two prints" println
"a" print space "b" println

"probe: if.false runs its branch when the condition is false" println
false { "if.false ran" println } if.false

"probe: execute. and !. take their target from the workbench" println
`dup .
1 execute. debug.display_stack
clear
`dup .
1 !. debug.display_stack
clear

"probe: return_from moves a named stack's top to the workbench" println
:t ensure_stack
@t
7
@main
:t return_from take println

"probe: rotate_stack_left and _right name their target" println
:t rotate_stack_left current println
:t rotate_stack_right current println

"probe: the workbench has its own dump" println
9 . debug.display_workbench
take drop

"probe: var- removes a variable binding" println
:x 42 var
:x var? println
:x var-

"probe: ?move sends a value to a named stack when its lambda says true" println
:m ensure_stack
@main
:m 5 { true } ?move
@m debug.display_stack
@main

"probe: fold_stack folds a named stack into a list, **in that stack**" println
:f ensure_stack
@f
1 2
@main
:f fold_stack
@f debug.display_stack
@main
